    words_note='Five words to carry through the course. A model is the thing that has learned patterns. A parameter is one adjustable setting inside it. Training adjusts those settings from many examples. Inference is using the trained model. And overfitting is when a model memorises its examples and fails on new ones. We meet every one of these again.',
    word_icons=['robot', 'switch', 'book', 'speech', 'cross'],
    cover_note='Welcome. Before we build anything, we spend one session on the ideas that sit under all of it: how AI and machine learning actually work, what the jobs and fields are, and why a company leader needs this picture. There are no exercises today. You will leave with a handbook to read before Session 1.',
    outcome_note='Here is what you leave with today. A clear picture of how AI works, how a model is measured and what happens behind a chat answer. A map of the fields, the jobs, the data and the costs behind AI work in a company. And your handbook, to read before Session 1. Nothing to submit and nothing to be tested on.',
    keep_note='Take the handbook home. It repeats today’s ideas with pictures and has a glossary you can search. Reading it is the only preparation for Session 1. Bring a laptop and an AI assistant account you already use, because some demonstrations let you join in. If anything today was unclear, write the question down. We start Session 1 by answering it.',
    recall=[],
